WEBVTT

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.230
<i>Yujin,</i>

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.800
<i>we probably would never have met</i>

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.520
<i>if it weren't for that picture, right?</i>

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.110
<i>To this day, I still regret it.</i>

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.380
<i>I never should have met you.</i>

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.250
<i>We should never have met.</i>

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.000
<i>One photograph led to the two of us meeting;</i>

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.070
<i>I had no idea back then</i>

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.700
<i>that these compiling coincidences</i>

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.370
<i>would cause us so much hardship in our lives.</i>

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:05.780
<i>Yujin,</i>

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.650
<i>let's never meet again.</i>

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.220
<i>Let's just cherish the time we spent at the sea as our last</i>

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.630
<i>and never meet again, savoring only the good times we had.</i>

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.340
The damage to your optic nerves was worse than we thought.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.400
You need surgery as soon as possible.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.300
Will I get better if I have the surgery?

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.860
There's no way of telling how much the hematoma has spread,

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.540
or what state it's in now.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.270
I don't care how you do it.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:21.380
As long as...

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.130
As long as I can hold on until <i>then.</i>

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.670
<i>You're really good at piano!</i>

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.350
<i>What's this song called?</i>

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:43.880
<i>"The First Time".</i>

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.070
<i>"The First Time"?</i>

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:12.040
<i>That was the first time I ditched class.</i>

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:17.110
<i>It was the first time I climbed over a fence on a guy's back,</i>

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.910
<i>and held hands with a guy.</i>

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:23.880
<i>It was also the first time I ever hopped on a bike with a guy.</i>

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.420
<i>Me too.</i>

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.490
Stop!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.900
Where the heck is this?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.740
Why didn't you wake me up?

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.280
What grade are you in?

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.040
I'm a second year.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.380
Aren't you scared of Gargamel?

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:31.120
I've never seen a second year with a pair of balls like you!

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.910
What's keeping you?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.890
Let's share a cab so it'll be cheaper.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.710
Hey, hurry up will you?

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:11.720
He's smoking...?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.400
Do it right!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.130
Yujin Jung!

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.910
I will not be late!

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.430
I will not be late!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.970
I will not be late!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:32.950
I will not...

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.450
Hurry up.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.090
I knew I was missing someone here.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.950
Go sit over there on your knees with your hands up.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.230
Why are <i>you</i> late when Sanghyuk got here on time?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.300
Don't get me started; this weird guy was—

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.800
You punk!

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.740
Do you have any idea what time it is?

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.810
It's that guy over there!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.810
Come here right now!

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:04.540
Would you look at this brat!

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.460
Do you think this is a joke?

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.180
He's quite charismatic, I'd say.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.420
He's cute.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:48.290
Hey Yujin,

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.410
he must be pretty smart if he transferred over

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.790
from a technical high school, right?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.430
I heard them talking about it in the teacher's lounge,

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.430
apparently Joonsang there was a go-getter at the technical high school too.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:03.540
What's it called again... the Math Olympics?

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.770
Don't you mean the Math Olympiad?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.940
Anyway, apparently he won first place there too.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.050
Joonsang's mine.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:14.280
Don't let me catch you guys so much as staring at him, okay?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.290
Joonsang Kang, was it?

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.390
Nice to meet you, I'm Sanghyuk Kim.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:24.890
Let's try to get along.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.030
You were supposed to have signed up for clubs today;

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:36.940
are you interested in anything in part—

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:37.910
Nope.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:46.890
Hey, Joonsang?

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.150
Joonsang Kang?

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.020
Hey, Sanghyuk,

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.120
what did I tell you?

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.690
You guys are totally incompatible.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.990
You're better off with a Virgo or a Capricorn.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.490
Here we go again.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:04.070
A lot of people might think zodiac signs are mere superstitions,

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.100
but it's actually a statistical science!

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.740
You could even call it a "life consulting" of sorts.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.270
Why don't you go study if you have the time to wiki that kind of—

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.240
Let me see that.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:14.760
I'll go ask him.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.010
I wonder how those two will work out.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.780
Joonsang is a Libra and Yujin is a Pisces, so...

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:25.630
He's less compatible with her than you.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:27.690
Actually, they're pretty much total opposites.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.430
Wait a second...

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.900
No. No way.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.970
Hey, Joonsang!

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.170
Joonsang!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.990
You need to be a little more cooperative;

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.640
otherwise, you'll cause trouble for the class president.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.050
Which club are you going to join?

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.260
So you don't fall asleep in school, huh?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.170
What?

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:05.160
Why don't you join the science club since you went to a tech school?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:07.660
I'm not really interested in clubs.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.400
Hey, Yujin?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.670
What club is <i>he</i> in?

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:14.800
Who?

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.370
You mean Sanghyuk?

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.640
He's in the radio club.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.060
Radio club, huh?

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:23.710
I'll join that then.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.280
What's going on?

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.220
I don't know.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.710
Oh no, I can't hear anything in there.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.150
Is it broken again? Let me see.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.050
I can't hear anything, Yongguk.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.620
What's broken now?

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:06.560
Try to assess the situation, will you?

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.350
We only have five minutes until lunch ends;

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.590
why don't you take a look at it, newbie?

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:14.000
I heard you joined the radio club as a joke.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.730
Me too.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.470
If you think you're so good, why don't you give it a try?

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.140
Would you guys stop it?

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:27.180
Joonsang.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:29.480
What the heck is he doing, Yongguk?

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.850
Does he really think he knows what's wrong?

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.520
Just leave it alone if you can't fix it; I'll do it.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:39.120
Radio club's no joke, newbie.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.010
You need to act more eager to learn

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:43.060
and not behave like you know everything already.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.030
You take a look at it.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:47.660
Is it this one here?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:50.870
Don't touch that!

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.030
What are you doing?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.540
Why the hell did you pull <i>all</i> the cords out?

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:57.170
It's going to be lunchtime soon, too.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.480
And now there's only three minutes until lunch.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.180
I can't even tell what's what!

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.790
Joonsang's a little strange, isn't he?

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:14.660
Hmm?

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:17.930
I think he joined the radio club because of you.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:21.260
No way. We just met today, remember?

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.230
I guess so.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:27.600
Yujin!

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:29.610
Get off of there; it's dangerous.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:33.280
No, I'm going to actually make it ten steps today, watch.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.880
I bet you won't even last ten steps.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.560
Just hold my hand already, Yujin.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.820
No.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.160
You're not my boyfriend.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:49.790
I'm not holding hands with you.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.560
I'm only going to hold hands with someone special.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:58.670
See that?

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.300
Tada.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:04.810
Come on.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:05.650
Wait up!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.610
My neck hurts now, Yujin.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:11.740
It really hurts.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.120
Can I stop now?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.090
Just sit a little longer; I'm almost done.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.590
I need to go pee, Yujin!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.270
I said hold still!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.630
You didn't forget that I did your homework for you, did you?

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:28.130
I'm going to start over if you flinch again.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.570
The phone's ringing!

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.100
Huijin!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.250
This one's so pretty; could you wrap it for me?

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:48.350
I think you'll look good in this; why not buy one?

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.850
This should be enough, shouldn't it?

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.220
I can't sell it that cheap...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.290
I'll come back again, okay?

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.220
O-Okay.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:54.830
See you.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.230
Thank you.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.160
Oh, you're here.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.610
You should put some more clothes on;

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:03.630
it's way too cold to be dressed like that.

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:04.480
Fine, fine.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.800
You should go home, Huijin's waiting for you.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.640
Okay. See you, Mom!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.290
How much is it?

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.230
Two dollars, please.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:33.360
You're a pretty young lady.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.550
Let me go!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.690
Come on, I'll buy you a drink.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.430
Why are you doing this?

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.360
Just come with me, will you?

00:16:38.570 --> 00:16:39.870
Mommy!

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:42.570
I'll buy you a drink, okay?!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:43.770
Let me go!

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:44.640
Yujin.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:45.810
Joonsang.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.810
Who is this guy?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.880
I don't know.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:51.320
Who are you?

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:52.750
Let her go.

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:55.250
How dare you talk to an adult like that?

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:58.920
Kids like you should just stay home and study!

00:16:59.060 --> 00:16:59.660
Let's go, Yujin.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.260
Hey, punk!

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:03.330
How dare you hit an adult?

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.330
Hey, come here!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.770
You little...

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.370
Are you out of your mind, bitch?

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.040
What do you want?

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:16.970
Joonsang!

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:19.410
Please stop!

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:33.330
I mean come on, we do have rules in this country, don't we?

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.930
Who's the real victim here?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:40.460
That young lady kept begging me to come drink with her,

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.500
but then I realized that she's a student.

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:43.400
Hey.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.670
I told her nicely to go back home to her parents,

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:51.780
but that punk came out of nowhere,

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:54.400
and then he punched me!

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.110
I'm the one who got hit here!

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.010
You're the one who hit him first!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.700
Be quiet, will you?

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.450
Is this any way to behave in a police station?

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:02.590
Oh, for Heaven's sake!

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.240
Not over there.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.270
Let me see.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.170
Hold still.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.940
Why did you even get involved when you can't fight?

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.310
Wipe your chin, will you?

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.380
My mom will be furious if she finds out—

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:28.220
Didn't I tell you two to call your parents?

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.750
What's the hold up?

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:33.490
Call your father and tell him to come here.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.890
He's not around.

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.060
Did he go somewhere?

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.270
He passed away.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:42.630
My mom's busy with work, too.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.130
What?

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.800
Did <i>you</i> call your parents?

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.970
Damn it, I don't have all day; call them now.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:51.320
Do you not speak Korean?

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.120
Your father.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.270
Call your father.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.240
He's not around.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.710
Damn it, these kids are driving me crazy.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.170
I didn't know you don't have a dad either.

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:27.810
My dad passed away from a disease.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.280
What about yours?

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.710
Do you like Sanghyuk?

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:35.980
Oh no, we're just friends.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:38.820
His dad was friends with my dad.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:41.820
Sanghyuk's dad and your dad?

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.100
They both graduated from our school.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.230
Isn't that something?

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.900
By the way, why did you transfer here?

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.330
To look for someone.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.370
Who?

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.040
No one worth mentioning.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.170
I'm going to head out.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.040
Bye.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.380
Hey, Joonsang!

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:09.750
Put that on your lips, three times a day!

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:10.620
Don't forget, okay?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:30.400
You're late.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.640
I thought you were going to be in Japan.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.950
I thought I'd stop by before the performance.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:42.680
When are you leaving?

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.320
Soon enough;

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.120
I reserved tickets for tomorrow.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:52.560
I'm going to bed.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.660
What were you doing out this late?

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.160
What happened to you?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.200
I just don't get it.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:05.410
Why did you want to go to school here, instead of going to America?

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:07.730
Why?

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.240
You went to school here too.

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.410
This school's full of your and Dad's cherished memories.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:17.680
And who <i>is</i> your father?

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.390
Who is he?

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.010
Your father's gone.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:25.060
He's dead.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:37.540
I'm heading for America as soon as this performance ends, okay?

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:58.060
Now think about it one more time...

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:00.830
and that should be enough.

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:03.380
I'm asking you all to try to understand this with your own minds,

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.130
not to take notes.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:08.270
All these formulae can be found in your textbooks.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:15.380
What's most important when it comes to mathematics,

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:17.560
is not simply elaborating on

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:19.110
already postulated hypotheses and formulae,

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:21.180
but to foster imagination and curiosity.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:24.790
Try looking at this empty blackboard and imagining the formula instead.

00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:28.790
Now it's time to solve a few practice problems;

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:31.330
any volunteers?

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:41.840
You over there.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.800
Why don't you give it a try?

00:22:44.270 --> 00:22:45.510
<i>Your father's gone.</i>

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:49.100
I just want to find out if you've understood the formula.

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:50.840
Don't be afraid to be wrong.

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:12.700
Do you mind if I ask who came up with this formula?

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:16.140
I just solved it my own way.

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:18.270
